From: ai_re sonic-nixos <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] orchagent: write SAI attribute values through the member that matches the attribute type

sai_attribute_value_t is a union. Writing value.u32 for a sai_uint16_t
attribute works on little-endian hosts only: on big-endian the SAI reads
value.u16, i.e. the upper half of the u32, which is 0. Found on ppc64 BE
(NXP T2080 + BCM56930), where every port/LAG PVID became 0.

Attribute types taken from the SAI headers (@type). Changed:
- portsorch.cpp: SAI_PORT_ATTR_PORT_VLAN_ID, SAI_LAG_ATTR_PORT_VLAN_ID
  (sai_uint16_t; was u32, also in the log lines)
- portsorch.cpp: SAI_PORT_ATTR_PATH_TRACING_TIMESTAMP_TYPE (enum, s32; was u16)
- intfsorch.cpp: SAI_ROUTER_INTERFACE_ATTR_NAT_ZONE_ID (sai_uint8_t; was u32), 2 places
- qosorch.cpp: SAI_WRED_ATTR_WEIGHT (sai_uint8_t; was s32, value 0)
- mirrororch.cpp: SAI_MIRROR_SESSION_ATTR_TOS (sai_uint8_t; was u16)
- mplsrouteorch.cpp: SAI_INSEG_ENTRY_ATTR_NUM_OF_POP (sai_uint8_t; was u32)
- dtelorch.cpp: SAI_DTEL_ATTR_LATENCY_SENSITIVITY (2 places),
  SAI_DTEL_INT_SESSION_ATTR_MAX_HOP_COUNT (sai_uint8_t; were u16)
- dash/dashhaorch.cpp: SAI_HA_SCOPE_ATTR_DASH_HA_ROLE (enum, s32; was u16)
- dash/dashorch.cpp: SAI_DASH_APPLIANCE_ATTR_LOCAL_REGION_ID (sai_uint8_t; was u32)
- dash/dashportmaporch.cpp: SAI_OUTBOUND_PORT_MAP_PORT_RANGE_ENTRY_ATTR_{MATCH,BACKEND}_PORT_BASE
  (sai_uint16_t; were u32), and the unit test reading them back
- dash/dashhafloworch.cpp: SAI_FLOW_ENTRY_BULK_GET_SESSION_FILTER_ATTR_INT_VALUE
  (sai_uint64_t; was u32)
Same-width mix-ups (enum via u32, u32 via s32) are harmless and left alone.

---
diff --git a/orchagent/dash/dashhafloworch.cpp b/orchagent/dash/dashhafloworch.cpp
index 9108a4d..831967c 100644
--- a/orchagent/dash/dashhafloworch.cpp
+++ b/orchagent/dash/dashhafloworch.cpp
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ sai_object_id_t FlowDumpFilterManager::createFilterSAI(const FlowDumpFilterEntry
                  filter_key == SAI_DASH_FLOW_ENTRY_BULK_GET_SESSION_FILTER_KEY_KEY_VERSION)
         {
             attrs[attr_count].id = SAI_FLOW_ENTRY_BULK_GET_SESSION_FILTER_ATTR_INT_VALUE;
-            attrs[attr_count].value.u32 = static_cast<uint32_t>(stoul(filter.value));
+            attrs[attr_count].value.u64 = stoull(filter.value);
             attr_count++;
         }
         else if (filter_key == SAI_DASH_FLOW_ENTRY_BULK_GET_SESSION_FILTER_KEY_SRC_IP_ADDR ||
